@prefix bl: <https://dagalog.no/ns/backlog#> .
@prefix ghissues: <https://github.com/daghovland/rdf-datalog/issues/> .
@prefix ghpull: <https://github.com/daghovland/rdf-datalog/pull/> .
@prefix prov: <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix session: <https://dagalog.no/ns/agentprov/session#> .

# PROSPECTIVE summary scaffold, generated by scripts/new-provenance-summary.sh.
# TODO: replace the placeholder summaryText/decisionPoint below with the
# actual distilled reasoning behind this PR before committing — see
# docs/plans/TRANSCRIPT_SUMMARY_GUIDELINES.md. Timestamps below are real
# (from `git log main..HEAD` on branch feat/390-runtime-ruleset-endpoint); everything else that
# isn't marked TODO can be left as-is.

ghpull:470 a bl:PullRequest, bl:WorkItem ;
    rdfs:label "sparql_endpoint: HTTP endpoint to load/replace a dataset's ruleset at runtime (#390)" ;
    bl:number 470 ;
    bl:state bl:Open ;
    bl:closesIssue ghissues:390 .

session:claudeSonnet5 a prov:SoftwareAgent ;
    rdfs:label "Claude Sonnet 5" .

session:pr470 a agp:AgentSession ;
    prov:wasAssociatedWith session:claudeSonnet5 ;
    prov:used ghissues:390 ;
    prov:startedAtTime "2026-08-12T22:47:17+02:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:endedAtTime "2026-08-12T21:07:17Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

session:pr470Summary a agp:TranscriptSummary ;
    agp:summaryText "Issue #390 asked for a runtime HTTP endpoint to load/replace a Datalog ruleset without restarting the server. Investigation of IncrementalReasoner (datalog crate) found apply_insertions/apply_deletions (facts) and apply_rule_deletions (existing-rule retraction), but no operation to add brand-new rules to a live reasoner incrementally — building that would touch the stratifier's topological ordering and was judged out of scope, matching the issue's own explicit allowance for a simpler full-replace endpoint. The harder problem turned out to be structural, not algorithmic: AppState.reasoner was a plain Option fixed at server startup, so no dataset created after startup (via POST /$/datasets, per the related issue #469) could ever gain a reasoner, and a dataset started without --rules could never gain one either. The fix was to wrap the reasoner in an interior-mutable Arc<RwLock<Option<...>>> cell and move that cell into DatasetRegistry per-dataset, so any dataset's ruleset can flip from absent to present after the fact. This also let dataset_state() drop the earlier Arc::ptr_eq aliasing special-case from #457 in favor of a structural guarantee. POST /{dataset}/rules reuses the existing datalog_parser and rebuilds via IncrementalReasoner::new over extensional-only facts, matching the pattern rebuild_from_base already used internally." ;
    agp:reasoningFor ghpull:470 ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy session:pr470 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo session:claudeSonnet5 .

session:pr470Summary agp:decisionPoint session:pr470Decision .

session:pr470Decision a agp:Decision ;
    agp:summaryText "Chose a full-ruleset-replace endpoint (parse new rules, strip the dataset to extensional facts, call IncrementalReasoner::new fresh) rather than per-ruleset-scoped named add/delete with a ruleset-id, which the issue also floated as its more ambitious version." ;
    agp:alternative "Per-ruleset-scoped add/delete (tracking a HashMap<RulesetId, Vec<Rule>> per dataset, retracting one ruleset via apply_rule_deletions while leaving siblings materialised) was rejected for this PR: it requires meaningfully more state design (id collision handling, cross-ruleset rule-dedup) and the issue itself explicitly sanctions the simpler full-replace fallback as already useful, so it was left as a follow-up rather than scope-creeping this PR." .
